{
  "id": "euler-totient-oq-02-oq-01",
  "title": "Euler Totient OQ-02-OQ-01: Factorization Product Formula",
  "description": "Records the Lean factorization/product-formula route for Euler's totient function using Mathlib's prime-factorization infrastructure.",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "Formalize Euler's totient product formula using Nat.factorization and product over prime factors.",
    "plain": "Express phi(n) as a product over prime-power contributions, then derive rational-form and density interpretations.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "The result connects multiplicativity of the totient function to Lean's canonical prime-factorization API.",
      "It gives concrete reusable formulas for computations and density-style interpretations of phi(n) / n."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "totient_factorization_formula proves the prime-factorization product formula for Nat.totient.",
      "totient_rational_formula rewrites the same result as a rational product over prime divisors.",
      "totient_div_primes_formula and totient_from_multiplicativity connect the formula to multiplicativity.",
      "totient_prime_power_contribution isolates the contribution of a prime power.",
      "totient_twelve_via_formula and totient_360 verify concrete examples.",
      "totient_density and totient_density_same_support package the phi(n) / n density interpretation."
    ],
    "open": [],
    "goal": "Expose the completed factorization-based totient formula and its computational corollaries."
  },
